1
00:00:01,918 --> 00:00:03,420
BOLORAM MUDULI: At home,

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:08,591
we husband and wife speak only in Gorum language.

3
00:00:09,551 --> 00:00:14,013
Hmm...when we meet with other peoples, we speak in Desia.

4
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,892
And when we meet Odia people, then we speak Odia.

5
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:22,063
OPINO GOMANGO IN ODIA:
'How you speak when you meet your own children outside?'

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,984
When we meet our children,

7
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:29,070
they speak in Odia with others...

8
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:31,489
We speak in Gorum language within ourselves.

9
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,161
With others we speak Odia.

10
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:41,458
'If it's your friend—a friend, friend from village,...

11
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:42,917
a guy from village...

12
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:45,044
how would you speak when you meet outside

13
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:47,630
or (and) how you'd speak in village?'

14
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:53,178
In our own caste (community), we speak in Gorum language.

15
00:00:53,887 --> 00:01:02,896
Hmm...with the town (urban) folks, we speak in Odia or Desia language.
